# CODEOWNERS — review routing for this repo.
#
# Intent (decision #20 analog, docs/knowledge-base/decisions.md): gate the
# high-blast-radius surfaces — every published package, the build/lint/CI
# tooling, and this file's own directory — behind a real review; leave the
# low-blast-radius surfaces (showcase demo pages, docs prose) free for agents
# and contributors to move fast in, same reasoning decision #20 applies to
# small products keeping demo/ in-repo: shared context, cheaper tokens, no
# production path at risk.
#
# `@fams/platform-team` is a PLACEHOLDER — no such GitHub team exists yet.
# The lines below are commented out so this file has zero enforcement effect
# until the team is created and these lines are uncommented (swap in the
# real team handle at that point, e.g. `@fams-org/platform-team`).
#
# # Every published package — component/token/build-pipeline changes.
# /packages/                              @fams/platform-team
#
# # Generation/check tooling (registry.json, llms.txt, token lint, …) — a
# # bug here silently breaks every package's gate.
# /scripts/                                @fams/platform-team
#
# # CI workflow + this file + the PR template — changing the gate itself.
# /.github/                                @fams/platform-team

# Showcase demo pages (/workshop/showcase/src/demos/) and docs (/docs/)
# are DELIBERATELY ABSENT from this file — low blast radius (a private
# preview app, not a published package; prose, not shipped code), so they
# stay free of a required-reviewer gate for agents and contributors. A
# pattern with no owner is a no-op in CODEOWNERS syntax, so "no owner" means
# "don't list it" here, not an empty-owner line.
